DDEEPPRREECCAATTIIOONN NNOOTTIICCEE
     kkeeyyllooggoouutt is deprecated and is not available as of FreeBSD 15.0.

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The kkeeyyllooggoouutt utility deletes the key stored by the key server process
     keyserv(8) to be used by any secure network services, such as NFS.  Fur‐
     ther access to the key is revoked, however current session keys may re‐
     main valid till they expire, or are refreshed.  This option will cause
     any background jobs that need secure RPC services to fail, and any sched‐
     uled aatt jobs that need the key to fail.  Also since only one copy is kept
     on a machine of the key, it is a bad idea to place this in your _._l_o_g_o_u_t
     file since it will affect other sessions on the same machine.

     The following option is available:

     --ff      Forget the rootkey.  This will break secure NFS if it is done on
             a server.

